      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "151df163-17d5-59da-9deb-38f2b2971a45",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Wojtek Memorial Trust\n- People: Wojtek\n- Roles: private, corporal\n- Places: Scotland, Hamadan, Iran, Soviet Union\n- Concepts: Scottish Charity, Polish II Corps, Second World War\n\nFacts:\n- Wojtek was born in 1942 and died in 1963.\n- Wojtek was a Syrian brown bear whose name is sometimes spelled \"Voytek\" in English.\n- Polish II Corps soldiers bought Wojtek as a young cub at a railroad station in Hamadan, Iran, after they had been evacuated from the Soviet Union.\n- Wojtek was officially enlisted as a soldier with the rank of private to provide for his rations and transportation, and he was later promoted to corporal.\n- The Wojtek Memorial Trust is a Scottish Charity with registration number SCO41057 that was established in 2009.\n- The Wojtek Memorial Trust was established to celebrate the life of Wojtek, the lives of those who knew him, and their stories during and after the Second World War.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
